---
import rawData from '../../data/deployment-topics.json';
import TopicLayout from '../../components/TopicLayout.astro';
import ScoreBar from '../../components/ScoreBar.astro';
import { type DeploymentData, type DeploymentRow, datasetLabel, intervalPct, intervalPp, modelLabel, pct, pp, seedProtocolLabel } from '../../data/topics';

const data = rawData as unknown as DeploymentData;
const fixed = data.rows.filter(row => row.track === 'pretraining-attribution-fixed');
const selected = data.rows.filter(row => row.track === 'pretraining-attribution-selected');
const contrasts = data.paired_contrasts.filter(row => row.track.startsWith('pretraining-attribution-'));
const controls = data.rows.filter(row => row.track === 'fixed-classical-control');
const models = ['labram','cbramod'];
const datasets = ['ds003810','physionet-eegmat-1.0.0'];
const settings = [
  { key: 'fixed', label: 'Fixed head · alpha 100', rows: fixed, track: 'pretraining-attribution-fixed' },
  { key: 'selected', label: 'Train-selected head · alpha 100 / 10,000 / 1', rows: selected, track: 'pretraining-attribution-selected' },
] as const;
const score = (rows: DeploymentRow[], model: string, dataset: string, initialization: string) => rows.find(row => row.model === model && row.dataset_id === dataset && row.initialization === initialization)!;
const contrast = (track: string, model: string, dataset: string) => contrasts.find(row => row.track === track && row.model === model && row.dataset_id === dataset)!;
const control = (dataset: string) => controls.find(row => row.dataset_id === dataset)!;
---
<TopicLayout
  title="Does pretraining help?"
  description="Matched pretrained and constructor-random LaBraM and CBraMod encoders on MI/rest and mental workload under fixed and train-selected readout settings."
  path="/topics/does-pretraining-help/"
  eyebrow="Representation controls · matched frozen encoders"
  dek="Sometimes. CBraMod gains under both readout settings on both tasks; LaBraM gains on mental workload and does not on MI/rest. These are matched frozen-encoder results, conditional on the tasks, splits and three constructor-random initializations—not a universal model ranking."
  activeSlug="does-pretraining-help"
>
  <section class="topic-section" aria-labelledby="contrast-heading">
    <div class="topic-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Paired attribution contrasts</p><h2 id="contrast-heading">Pretrained minus random, with the head held honest</h2></div><p>Each constructor-random architecture is averaged over three initialization seeds. Pretrained and random encoders share the same splits, pooling and ridge readout protocol.</p></div>
    <div class="topic-table scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Pretraining attribution contrasts, scrolls horizontally">
      <table><caption>Difference in participant-mean balanced accuracy. Intervals are paired participant bootstraps, conditional on three random initializations.</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Task / model</th><th scope="col">Fixed alpha 100</th><th scope="col">Train-selected alpha</th></tr></thead><tbody>{datasets.flatMap(dataset => models.map(model => {
        const fixedContrast = contrast('pretraining-attribution-fixed',model,dataset);
        const selectedContrast = contrast('pretraining-attribution-selected',model,dataset);
        return <tr><th scope="row">{modelLabel(model)}<small>{datasetLabel(dataset)} · n={fixedContrast.participants}</small></th><td><span class="metric">{pp(fixedContrast.difference, 2)}</span><span class="interval">{intervalPp(fixedContrast.paired_participant_bootstrap_95, 2)}</span><ScoreBar value={Math.abs(fixedContrast.difference)} max={0.12} label={`${pp(fixedContrast.difference,2)} pretraining contrast`} tone={fixedContrast.difference >= 0 ? 'olive' : 'ink'} /></td><td><span class="metric">{pp(selectedContrast.difference, 2)}</span><span class="interval">{intervalPp(selectedContrast.paired_participant_bootstrap_95, 2)}</span><ScoreBar value={Math.abs(selectedContrast.difference)} max={0.12} label={`${pp(selectedContrast.difference,2)} pretraining contrast`} tone={selectedContrast.difference >= 0 ? 'olive' : 'ink'} /></td></tr>;
      }))}</tbody></table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="topic-section" aria-labelledby="scores-heading">
    <div class="topic-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Measured scores</p><h2 id="scores-heading">Both readout settings stay visible</h2></div><p>Head selection uses only inner training participants. Showing both settings prevents a test score from choosing the adaptation budget after the fact.</p></div>
    {settings.map(setting => <div class="topic-table topic-table-spaced scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={`${setting.label} pretrained and random encoder scores, scrolls horizontally`}>
      <table><caption>{setting.label} · participant-mean balanced accuracy.</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Task / model</th><th scope="col">Pretrained encoder</th><th scope="col">Random encoder mean</th><th scope="col">Paired difference</th></tr></thead><tbody>{datasets.flatMap(dataset => models.map(model => {
        const pretrained = score(setting.rows,model,dataset,'pretrained');
        const random = score(setting.rows,model,dataset,'constructor-random-mean');
        const delta = contrast(setting.track,model,dataset);
        return <tr><th scope="row">{modelLabel(model)}<small>{datasetLabel(dataset)}</small></th><td><span class="metric">{pct(pretrained.value)}</span></td><td><span class="metric">{pct(random.value)}</span><small>3 initializations</small></td><td><span class="metric">{pp(delta.difference,2)}</span><span class="interval">{intervalPp(delta.paired_participant_bootstrap_95,2)}</span></td></tr>;
      }))}</tbody></table>
    </div>)}
    <div class="evidence-grid">{datasets.map(dataset => {
      const row = control(dataset);
      return <article class="evidence-card"><p class="eyebrow">Fixed classical control</p><div class="reading">{pct(row.value)}</div><ScoreBar value={row.value} label={`${pct(row.value)} balanced accuracy`} tone="ink"/><p>{modelLabel(row.model)} · {datasetLabel(dataset)}</p><small>95% interval {intervalPct(row.confidence_interval_95)}</small></article>;
    })}</div>
  </section>

  <section class="topic-section" aria-labelledby="seed-heading">
    <div class="topic-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Training-seed sensitivity</p><h2 id="seed-heading">A spread is not a confidence interval</h2></div><p>Five existing EEGNet protocols were rerun with three fixed MPS seeds. The range is a small-sample training sensitivity check; it does not replace the published point estimate or describe population uncertainty.</p></div>
    <div class="topic-table scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="EEGNet three-seed sensitivity results, scrolls horizontally">
      <table><caption>Balanced accuracy across three training seeds. Sample SD and full range are percentage points.</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Protocol</th><th scope="col">Three runs</th><th scope="col">Mean</th><th scope="col">Sample SD</th><th scope="col">Full range</th></tr></thead><tbody>{data.seed_sensitivity.map(group => <tr><th scope="row">{seedProtocolLabel(group.protocol)}<small>n={group.participants} · {group.trials.toLocaleString('en-US')} trials</small></th><td>{group.runs.map(run => pct(run.balanced_accuracy,2)).join(' / ')}</td><td><span class="metric">{pct(group.mean_balanced_accuracy,2)}</span></td><td>{(group.sample_standard_deviation*100).toFixed(2)} pp</td><td>{(group.full_range*100).toFixed(2)} pp<small>{pct(group.minimum,2)}–{pct(group.maximum,2)}</small></td></tr>)}</tbody></table>
    </div>
    <p class="citation-note">Dataset authors, versions, licenses and source records for all four seed-sensitivity datasets are listed under <a href="/data-use/#sources">Data use &amp; privacy → Sources in this release</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="topic-section" id="methods-and-limits" aria-labelledby="limits-heading">
    <div class="topic-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Methods &amp; limits</p><h2 id="limits-heading">What a positive contrast establishes</h2></div><p>These controls narrow one question: whether the pretrained initialization helps this frozen architecture, split and readout relative to constructor-random encoders.</p></div>
    <div class="method-grid-wide">
      <article><h3>Fixed versus selected heads</h3><p>The primary head fixes ridge alpha at 100. The sensitivity setting selects among 100, 10,000 and 1 using inner training participants only. Both are reported.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Three seeds, one cohort</h3><p>The random baseline averages three encoder initializations. Those are not three independent datasets, and the participant bootstrap does not include unrestricted retraining uncertainty.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Task-specific evidence</h3><p>MI/rest contains 10 participants and 1,200 trials; mental workload contains 36 participants and 2,160 trials. A method can rank only within a compatible protocol.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Exposure is unresolved</h3><p>The comparison does not establish that the benchmarks were unseen during pretraining. It also does not certify a universal benefit across tasks or adaptation budgets.</p></article>
    </div>
    <div class="citation-list">
      <article><h3>MI / rest · OpenNeuro ds003810 v2.0.2</h3><p>Peterson et al. · CC0-1.0.</p><p><a href="https://doi.org/10.18112/openneuro.ds003810.v2.0.2" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Dataset record ↗</a></p></article>
      <article><h3>Mental workload · EEGMAT 1.0.0</h3><p>Zyma et al. · Open Data Commons Attribution License 1.0.</p><p><a href="https://physionet.org/content/eegmat/1.0.0/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">PhysioNet record ↗</a></p></article>
    </div>
    <p class="citation-note">Data source: <a href="/data/deployment-topics.json" download>reviewed aggregate JSON</a> · schema {data.schema_version} · generated {data.generated_at.slice(0,10)}.</p>
  </section>
</TopicLayout>
